1. OHDSI CommonDataModel (https://github.com/OHDSI/CommonDataModel, tag v5.5.0; Apache-2.0)
   Used in: examples/synthea_omop/package/target/tables.json, field_docs.json, field_domains.json, provenance.json
   What: the table and column definitions of the OMOP CDM v5.4 and the text of OMOP_CDMv5.4_Field_Level.csv and the table-level CSV of the same tag
         (user guidance, ETL conventions, foreign-key domains, table descriptions).
   Changes: reformatted into JSON; the text is word for word. Empty values written as NA in the CSV are kept as NA.

2. dbt-synthea (https://github.com/OHDSI/dbt-synthea; Apache-2.0)
   Used in: examples/synthea_omop/package/source/tables.json, matches/matches.json, and examples/synthea_omop/reference/recipes/, reference/fields/
   - source/tables.json: the column descriptions are copied from models/staging/synthea/_synthea__models.yml; the column names and types are those of the Synthea CSV files.
   - matches/matches.json: matches of source columns to target columns derived from the SQL lineage of the dbt-synthea models (some matches were made noisy on purpose).
   - reference/recipes and reference/fields: the reference conversion, derived from the compiled SQL of the dbt-synthea models, split per target table and column; alignment data added by this project.
   Changes: the original files were not copied unchanged. They were reformatted, split, annotated and combined. They are not endorsed by the dbt-synthea project.

3. dbtpcdi (https://github.com/rlsalcido24/dbtpcdi; Apache-2.0)
   Used in: benchmarks/tpcdi/gold_crosscheck/dbt_port.sql, normalize.sql
   What: the dbt models of an independent TPC-DI implementation (Snowflake), used as a cross-check of the TPC-DI gold.
   Changes: ported to DuckDB and run on the parsed Source.* tables; Batch-1 history load only; not endorsed by the dbtpcdi project.

4. Not included, so not covered by this notice: the Synthea sample data, the OMOP vocabulary seed files, and the reference tables built from them (see LICENSES.md).
